 "description": "DIRECTED, BOND-COUPLED CONDUCT (block 281000). The affordance vocabulary (280000) offers agent-directed actions whenever a target is in range; these rules make WHOM you act on read the held Bond (277000). Each directed action's DEEP (plan_value) score = plan_base + a coupling to the Bond's affect toward its target: harm rises with resentment and falls with affection; help/transfer rise with affection. The FAST pull (impulse = vocabulary base_weight; harm LOW, help HIGH) is unchanged -- the Bond only shapes the model-based re-score, so the decision core (279000) collapse directs harm at a resented rival (not a friend) and giving/aid toward the cared-for, while violence stays rare. Reading held affect is a RULE (graph read), not adapter arithmetic. FALSIFIER: conduct_resent_gain = conduct_affection_gain = 0 collapses plan_value to plan_base -> no directedness (rival indistinguishable from friend). Gains are knobs on the ConductState. ZERO new Rust; self_load_only.",
